# L §5.14 (round 8): "on d is the movement's day, s.day: a date, a window (§4.4), a hole, or none, which gives no
# instance at that key". gift[ana]'s day is a none row, so it has no instance: flows of the move count gift[ben]
# only, 10.00 PLN, and a count of the move's movements in 2026 is 1. (Settles writer 4's gap 5, L §4.2 vs L §5.14.)
=== m.tally
model g
  tally 2
  on 2026-10-20
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source s "s"
unit PLN: currency minor 0.01

index people = [ana, ben]
kind gifts: event certain
  leg cash: PLN

place konto: accounts PLN lives 2026-01-01..
place world: outside lives 1900-01-01..

input gday[p in people]: date
input amt: money PLN

move gift[p in people]: gifts
  on gday[p]
  leg cash from world to konto amount amt

ask f: flows(gift, 2026)
ask n: count(g in gifts over 2026)

version v
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2025-12-01
  gday[ana] = none
  gday[ben] = 2026-03-01
  amt = 10.00 PLN
  opening[konto] = 0.00 PLN at 2026-01-01 start "bilans"
=== expect
f: 10.00 PLN
...
n: 1
...
